# Naman IAS Academy — Core

Premium UPSC/IAS education platform (portal + public site + admin) for Naman Sharma IAS Academy. Users: aspirants, enrolled students, parents, admins, ops.

## Canonical layout

- `app/(site)/` — public marketing (ISR-first; layout must not read cookies/DB)
- `app/(portal)/` / `app/portal/` — buyer/student portal
- `app/admin/` — staff admin
- `app/api/` — route handlers
- `lib/` — domain logic (`dataProvider`, entitlements, payments, store, sms, telegram, analytics)
- `components/public/` — public UI; `components/admin/` — admin UI
- `supabase/migrations/` — schema source of truth
- `docs/notes-store-spec.md` — Notes Store requirements (authoritative)

## Architecture facts

- Next.js 14 App Router, Supabase (service role server-side), ICICI Eazypay for money
- Design: Sora (heading) + Inter (body); tokens in `app/globals.css` + `tailwind.config.ts`
- Public chrome: `PublicNav` hydrates auth via `/api/session/state` — do not break ISR by reading sessions in `(site)/layout`

## Before changing code

1. Inspect existing consumers and data flow.
2. Reuse Academy patterns; do not invent parallel systems.
3. Prefer smallest fix over rewrite.
4. Never expose/commit secrets.

## Sensitive — inspect first, change rarely

Auth/sessions · `payments` / fee-state / entitlements · lecture access · quiz gates · Eazypay (`lib/eazypay.ts`) · Telegram event types/`*/2` · DLT SMS · Notes Store isolation (`store_*`, `NIASN-N-`) · PublicNav session hydration · LecturePlayer

## Notes Store (summary)

Physical printed notes, guest checkout, store-owned Eazypay Verify, kill switch `notes_store`. Never write academy `payments`/`students`/`buyers`/`leads`. Spec: `docs/notes-store-spec.md`. Isolation guard: `scripts/ci/guard-store-domain-isolation.mjs`.

